  "final_text": "**Proposed disposition:** CLOSE_FP, confidence 0.70. This is a proposal, and a human analyst decides.\n\n**Three facts that drove it:**\n1. The large BUY order O-00017411 was 19,570 shares, 7.96x depth. It was working. 3,568 shares (18.2%) filled in two partial fills at 12:29:00 and 12:29:04, before the trader's only opposite-side trade. That meets the genuine-execution test, so feature (a) (an order not meant to execute) is absent.\n2. The opposite-side trade was a single SELL of 587 at 12:29:12, much smaller than the earlier same-side fills. The 14,437 reduction two seconds later is ordinary management of a working order, so feature (b) (a benefit from the opposite-side trade) is not established.\n3. There is no repetition (repetitions_in_session is 0) and no prior alerts. There are no market events in the window and no registered market making. The only supported explanation is genuine execution of the resting order.\n\n**What would change my mind:** evidence that the 587 SELL exploited a price move created by the resting bid. Examples are reversion after the reduction, or the same pattern in other sessions. The price did move +2 ticks in the trader's favour and the order was one-sided, but no reversion was measured.",
